<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adelaide</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adelaide is the capital of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, on the plains between Gulf St Vincent and the Mount Lofty Ranges. Founded in 1836 and laid out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-light">Colonel William Light</a> on a grid of streets surrounded by parklands, it was named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-of-saxe-meiningen">Queen Adelaide</a>. It grew as the centre of a planned colony of free settlers without convicts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adelaide.jpg" alt="Adelaide" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ardash Muradian from Australia; derivative work by Georgfotoart · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adelaide_skyline,_December_2022_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
